# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (secrets) — but keep the example template
.env*
!.env.local.example

# real student data used as parser fixtures (PII — keep out of git)
/fixtures/

# Working files at the repo root that hold real data. These were untracked
# but NOT ignored, so a single `git add -A` would have committed them
# permanently. Specifically:
#   - /Screenshots/ — source images for public/help/calendar-link.html.
#     Three of them ("Publish", "ICS", "Copy Link") show a real, live
#     Outlook ICS subscription URL in readable text. That URL is an
#     unauthenticated, permanent feed of one person's calendar, including
#     class titles and locations. It must never enter git history, where
#     it would survive any later deletion.
#   - /host ICS.ics, /host schedule by block.xls, /Test Report-test.xlsx —
#     real student schedules and a real report export.
#   - /PRD Notes.docx — internal planning notes.
/Screenshots/
/host ICS.ics
/host schedule by block.xls
/Test Report-test.xlsx
/PRD Notes.docx

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Claude Code session config (user-specific)
.claude/
